# A100 deployment parameters (compute capability 8.0): the same parameters as configs/h100.env — the two interpreters, the checkpoint, the
# JIT cache root — with the target-GPU label A100; this file sets the label and reads the rest through configs/h100.env, so the two
# configurations cannot drift. No variable here is card-specific: the levers select their compute-capability-8.0 kernel rows at run time from
# the running GPU (opt_core's tables and the kit's per-card rows). What differs from a 9.0 card — each difference is named on the run's
# LEVER / XTR / SELECT lines (STOCK.md "Cards"); anything not listed is the same code path and the same lever set:
#   1. fpf_trimul (fast, big): the TriMul launch cells are the 8.0 rows of opt_core's one cell table (pointer-load tiles; the 9.0 cells use TMA loads).
#   2. mkdit (fast): the megakernel's sm_80 tile row `mkdit.CONFIGS[(8, 0)]`; its token floor is the same on both cards.
#   3. xtr (exact): the transition provider's exact tier serves the 128-wide pair transitions (`128x512` / `128x256`) on the fused row from its
#      size floor up; smaller calls, the 384-wide single transition and the c=64 tracks run stock's statements BY NAME (`route:<key>:<word>`).
#   4. opt_core's fused-LayerNorm / transition tiles and triangle-attention cells: their 8.0 rows; a LayerNorm size without a tile row autotunes
#      its tiles at the first call of that size (slower first item, same outputs), as on 9.0.
#   5. fpf_gflash (fast): the fused triangle attention's core asks the provider's tier word `fast` on both cards (`rf3fpf/fpf_rf3_triattn.CARD_ROWS`);
#      on 8.0 that resolves to the provider's Triton kernel at the pair track and to the stock op by name at the template track's small-size cell
#      (the provider's CUDA kernels are sm_90-only) — same numerics class; the `[fpf_rf3 triattn] SELECT ... cc=8.0 ...` line names the row.
#   6. fpf_msa (fast, big): the MSA-module component binds `rf3fpf/fpf_rf3_msa_rows.CARD_ROWS[(8, 0)]` = the pair-weighted-averaging cell alone;
#      the outer-product-mean statement stays stock's on this card, named on the record (`FPF APPLIED ... msa_units=['pwa'] msa_aside={'opm': 'cc8.0:...'}`).
#   7. fpf_tg (fast): no pairformer CUDA graph at any size on 8.0 (`tgbudget.CARD_BUDGETS[(8, 0)]['fast'] = 0`): the fast arm's pair-bias attention
#      row on sm_80 allocates workspace inside the capture, which invalidates it, so every trunk call takes the uncaptured forward BY NAME
#      (`skipped:<n>`; EXIT `levers_budget_skipped=fpf_tg(max_i=0,...)`, exit 0); exact's stock-kernel arm captures on 8.0 as on 9.0.
# A lever of a mode that cannot engage at all on the running GPU (no row for its compute capability, a kernel that does not build) refuses the run by
# name (exit 1 / NOT ACTIVE exit 3); `--mode off` runs stock. Documented size gates are census, exit 0.
# usage: `run.sh pred|check|warm|install --config a100 [--mode <mode>] ...`, or `source configs/a100.env` before calling the package directly.
export MODEL_OPT_TARGET_GPU=${MODEL_OPT_TARGET_GPU:-A100}                                                            # the GPU this configuration targets (compute capability 8.0); check notes a mismatch with the visible GPU
source "$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)/h100.env"                                                         # every other parameter, and this file's exit status (the package's refusal, rc 3, propagates)
